---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
import SvgDefs from "../components/SvgDefs.astro"
import ThemeToggle from "../components/ThemeToggle.astro"
import Message from "../components/Message.astro"
import { apiBase, loginUrl } from "../lib/config"

// URLs derive from astro.config.mjs's site so the @id cross-reference always
// matches the Organization entity BaseHead emits.
const site = Astro.site!
const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
    name: "Threa",
    url: site.href,
    description:
      "Team chat with memory at its core: decisions and their reasoning become searchable memos linked to the conversation. Open source, with a public REST API and bot runtime for connecting your own agents.",
    applicationCategory: "BusinessApplication",
    operatingSystem: "Web",
    softwareHelp: { "@type": "CreativeWork", url: new URL("/developers", site).href },
    publisher: { "@id": new URL("/#organization", site).href },
  },
]
---

<Layout schema={schema}>
  <SvgDefs />

<div class="frame">
  <div class="hero-shell">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div class="nav-row" data-decorative>
        <div class="brand">
          <svg><use href="#threa-mark"/></svg>
          <span class="wordmark">Threa</span>
        </div>
        <nav class="nav-links">
          <a href="/" aria-current="page">Product</a><a href="/about">About</a><a href="/developers">Developers</a>
        </nav>
        <a class="nav-login" href={loginUrl}>Log in</a>
        <ThemeToggle />
      </div>
      <div class="hero-stage">
        <div>
          <h1 class="h-display">
            Chat that remembers the decisions.
          </h1>
          <p class="lede">
            Team chat with a memory underneath. When your team settles
            something, the decision and the why stay attached to the messages,
            so when the question comes back in three months there's an answer
            instead of a re-litigation. I built this because chat kept eating
            mine.
          </p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="cta" href="#waitlist">Join the waitlist</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-right" data-decorative>
          <ol class="thread" aria-label="A decision made on March 12, kept as a memo, and answered on May 7">
            <li class="stop is-then">
              <p class="stop-head"><time class="stop-date" datetime="2026-03-12">Mar 12</time><span class="stop-where">#api-v3</span></p>
              <Message author="jordan" time="11:42">
                <div class="tl-text">hold on, I'm not comfortable changing the auth boundary without working through the token-rotation flow first. can we pause this?</div>
              </Message>
              <Message author="maya" time="11:44">
                <div class="tl-text">Fair. Let's hold v3 until you've walked us through it.</div>
              </Message>
            </li>
            <li class="stop is-kept">
              <div class="memory-card decision-memo">
                <div class="dm-kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Decision</div>
                <div class="dm-title">Auth refactor held pending token-rotation review.</div>
                <div class="dm-body">Migrating live sessions would force everyone to sign in again. Jordan walks through the rotation flow first.</div>
                <div class="dm-source">Kept from 3 messages in <span class="ref-pill">#api-v3</span></div>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="stop is-now">
              <p class="stop-head"><time class="stop-date" datetime="2026-05-07">May 7</time><span class="stop-where">#sprint-planning</span></p>
              <Message author="maya" time="09:12">
                <div class="tl-text"><span class="mention">@ariadne</span> we're picking auth back up this sprint. Why did we hold it?</div>
              </Message>
              <Message author="ariadne" time="09:12">
                <div class="tl-text">You paused v3 on Mar 12 until Jordan reviewed the token-rotation model. That walkthrough hasn't happened yet.</div>
              </Message>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="frame">
  <div class="memo-shell value-shell">
    <ul class="value-grid">
      <li>
        <h3>Every channel is also a board</h3>
        <p>The same messages, grouped by topic. A discussion from three weeks ago is one card away instead of a scroll away.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Ask what was decided</h3>
        <p>Threa keeps decisions and context as short memos linked to the messages they came from. Ask Ariadne, or search, and get the memo with its sources.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Plug in your own agent</h3>
        <p>Claude Code, Codex, Pi, or one you wrote. Connect it as a bot and it reads the room, answers mentions, and posts its work back.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Open source</h3>
        <p>The whole product is public. It's MIT licensed so you can help fixing what I broke. <a href="https://github.com/threahq/threa">It's on GitHub.</a></p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================
     BOARD — the same channel, two ways
     A frameless side-by-side: the stream (flat, on the paper, with a
     floating composer) vs the board (real conversation cards). Same
     messages both sides. Reuses the timeline-demo vocabulary (.tl-row,
     .tl-avatar, .mention, .reactions, .trace-card, .recall-memo-card,
     composer parts) so it tracks the hero.
     ============================================================ -->
<div class="frame warm" id="board">
  <div class="memo-shell board-shell">
    <h2>Chat you can find later.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      A timeline is good for keeping up. It's bad for finding a discussion again
      three weeks later. The board is the same channel grouped by topic, so you
      open the conversation instead of scrolling for it.
    </p>

    <div class="board-compare" data-decorative>
      <!-- STREAM: flat feed on the paper, composer pinned to the bottom -->
      <div class="board-col is-stream">
        <div class="board-lens"><span class="k">Stream</span><span class="m">#product, as it happened</span></div>

        <Message author="maya" time="14:03">
          <div class="tl-text">Picking the auth refactor back up next sprint. Anyone remember why we paused it in March?</div>
        </Message>

        <Message author="sam" time="14:04">
          <div class="tl-text">empty states for the board are on staging now. the board one especially came out nice</div>
          <div class="reactions"><span class="rxn"><span class="em">🙌</span><span class="num">2</span></span></div>
        </Message>

        <Message author="jordan" time="14:05">
          <div class="tl-text">pretty sure there were open concerns but I can't find the thread lol</div>
          <div class="board-prov"><svg><use href="#icon-layers"/></svg><span>continues <span class="topic">Auth refactor: pause or push?</span></span><span class="sep">·</span><span>2m</span></div>
        </Message>

        <Message author="alex" time="14:05">
          <div class="tl-text">shit, uh 🤷 <span class="mention">@ariadne</span> ?</div>
        </Message>

        <div class="trace-card is-static">
          <div class="trace-icon-slot">
            <div class="trace-icon trace-icon-running" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#spinner-icon"/></svg></div>
            <div class="trace-icon trace-icon-done" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#check-icon"/></svg></div>
          </div>
          <div class="trace-main">
            <div class="trace-row trace-row-running"><div class="trace-title">Ariadne is working…</div><div class="trace-sub">searching</div></div>
            <div class="trace-row trace-row-done"><div class="trace-title">Session complete</div><div class="trace-sub">5 steps · 3.7s</div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="trace-time">14:05</div>
        </div>

        <Message author="ariadne" time="14:05">
          <div class="tl-text">You paused it for Jordan's review of the token-rotation model. The concern was migrating live sessions without a forced re-auth.</div>
        </Message>

      </div>

      <!-- center gutter: "same messages" (stands horizontal on mobile) -->
      <div class="board-gutter"><div class="board-badge"><span class="ic"><svg><use href="#icon-swap"/></svg></span><span class="lbl">same messages</span></div></div>

      <!-- BOARD: the same messages grouped into two topic cards -->
      <div class="board-col">
        <div class="board-lens"><span class="k">Board</span><span class="m">#product, by topic</span></div>
        <div class="board-list">
          <div class="board-card">
            <div class="board-card-title">
              <svg class="chev"><use href="#icon-chevron"/></svg>
              <span class="title">Auth refactor: pause or push?</span>
              <span class="unread-dot"></span>
              <span class="board-hbtn" aria-label="Open conversation"><svg><use href="#icon-panelright"/></svg></span>
              <span class="board-hbtn" aria-label="More"><svg><use href="#icon-morevert"/></svg></span>
            </div>
            <div class="board-locator"><span class="board-tile"><svg><use href="#icon-hash"/></svg></span><span class="lstream">product</span><span class="sep">·</span><span>now</span></div>
            <div class="board-card-body">
              <Message author="maya" time="14:03">
                <div class="tl-text">Picking the auth refactor back up next sprint. Anyone remember why we paused it in March?</div>
              </Message>
              <Message author="jordan" time="14:05">
                <div class="tl-text">pretty sure there were open concerns but I can't find the thread lol</div>
              </Message>
              <Message author="alex" time="14:05">
                <div class="tl-text">shit, uh 🤷 <span class="mention">@ariadne</span> ?</div>
              </Message>
              <div class="trace-card is-static">
                <div class="trace-icon-slot">
                  <div class="trace-icon trace-icon-running" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#spinner-icon"/></svg></div>
                  <div class="trace-icon trace-icon-done" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#check-icon"/></svg></div>
                </div>
                <div class="trace-main">
                  <div class="trace-row trace-row-running"><div class="trace-title">Ariadne is working…</div><div class="trace-sub">searching</div></div>
                  <div class="trace-row trace-row-done"><div class="trace-title">Session complete</div><div class="trace-sub">5 steps · 3.7s</div></div>
                </div>
                <div class="trace-time">14:05</div>
              </div>
              <Message author="ariadne" time="14:05">
                <div class="tl-text">You paused it for Jordan's review of the token-rotation model.</div>
                <div class="recall-memo-card">
                  <div class="rmc-icon"><svg><use href="#icon-compass"/></svg></div>
                  <div class="rmc-body">
                    <div class="rmc-kicker"><span class="k-type">decision</span><span class="k-tag">#product</span></div>
                    <div class="rmc-title">Auth refactor held pending token-rotation review</div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="rmc-meta">Mar 12</div>
                </div>
              </Message>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="board-card">
            <div class="board-card-title">
              <svg class="chev"><use href="#icon-chevron"/></svg>
              <span class="title">Empty states shipped to staging</span>
              <span class="dot-slot"></span>
              <span class="board-hbtn" aria-label="Open conversation"><svg><use href="#icon-panelright"/></svg></span>
              <span class="board-hbtn" aria-label="More"><svg><use href="#icon-morevert"/></svg></span>
            </div>
            <div class="board-locator"><span class="board-tile"><svg><use href="#icon-hash"/></svg></span><span class="lstream">product</span><span class="sep">·</span><span>now</span></div>
            <div class="board-card-body">
              <Message author="sam" time="14:04">
                <div class="tl-text">empty states for the board are on staging now. the board one especially came out nice</div>
                <div class="reactions"><span class="rxn"><span class="em">🙌</span><span class="num">2</span></span></div>
              </Message>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================
     MEMORY FLOW — capture · hold · return
     Mirrors the real mechanic: extract a decision from the
     conversation, hold it as a memo, retrieve it when someone asks
     about the topic again. No invented graph relations.
     ============================================================ -->
<div class="frame">
  <div class="memo-shell">
    <h2>Decisions get kept. Lunch orders don't.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Threa reads the conversation, keeps the lines where the team settled
      something, and saves them as short memos linked to the messages they
      came from. When the question comes up again, Ariadne finds the memo and
      the conversation behind it.
    </p>

    <div class="memory-flow">

      <!-- ============ 01 · CAPTURE ============ -->
      <div class="memory-col">
        <h3 class="memory-heading"><span class="n">1</span>Capture what matters</h3>
        <p class="memory-why">
          Most of a channel is noise. The parts worth keeping are usually a
          handful of lines where the team settles something, works out a process,
          or shares context they'll need again.
        </p>

        <div class="capture-list" data-decorative aria-label="Five-message slice; the three middle messages carry the decision.">
          <Message author="sam" time="11:38" class="is-noise">
            <div class="tl-text">lunch order, pasta or pizza. last call</div>
          </Message>

          <Message author="jordan" time="11:42">
            <div class="tl-text">hold on, I'm not comfortable changing the auth boundary without working through the token-rotation flow first. can we pause this until I've reviewed the design</div>
          </Message>

          <Message author="maya" time="11:44">
            <div class="tl-text">Fair. Let's hold v3 then. What do you need from us before sign-off?</div>
          </Message>

          <Message author="jordan" time="11:46">
            <div class="tl-text">a walkthrough of the rotation flow + how existing sessions migrate. I'll block out time the week of the 18th</div>
          </Message>

          <Message author="sam" time="11:47" class="is-noise">
            <div class="tl-text">pizza it is, ordering now</div>
          </Message>

        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- ============ 02 · HOLD ============ -->
      <div class="memory-col">
        <h3 class="memory-heading"><span class="n">2</span>Hold it as a memo</h3>
        <p class="memory-why">
          Nobody rereads a transcript two months later. A short, sourced memo is
          the part that stays useful once the thread has scrolled away.
        </p>

        <div class="memory-card decision-memo" data-decorative>
          <div class="dm-kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Decision · Mar 12</div>
          <div class="dm-title">Auth refactor held pending token-rotation review.</div>

          <div class="dm-field">
            <div class="dm-label">Why</div>
            <div class="dm-body">Jordan asked to pause the v3 auth boundary until the rotation flow has been walked through. The concern was migrating existing sessions without a forced re-auth wave.</div>
          </div>

          <div class="dm-field">
            <div class="dm-label">Next</div>
            <div class="dm-body">Design walkthrough with Jordan, week of Apr 18.</div>
          </div>

          <div class="dm-field">
            <div class="dm-label">Source</div>
            <div class="dm-body dm-source">3 messages · <span class="ref-pill">#api-v3</span> · Jordan Lee · Maya Reyes</div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- ============ 03 · RETURN ============ -->
      <div class="memory-col is-return">
        <h3 class="memory-heading"><span class="n">3</span>Return when it comes up again</h3>
        <p class="memory-why">
          A reason you can't find isn't worth much. When the question returns,
          ask Ariadne to search for the relevant memo and follow its links back to
          the source conversation.
        </p>

        <div class="recall-thread" data-decorative>
          <div class="recall-meta">
            <span class="hash">#sprint-planning</span>
            <span>May 7, two months later</span>
          </div>

          <div class="recall-list">
            <Message author="maya" time="09:12">
              <div class="tl-text"><span class="mention">@ariadne</span> we're picking auth back up this sprint. What was the hold on again?</div>
            </Message>

            <Message author="ariadne" time="09:12">
              <div class="tl-text">
                You paused v3 in March pending Jordan's review of the rotation flow.
                Wei flagged a related mobile-session concern in April that didn't make
                the original hold. Worth folding in before the walkthrough.
              </div>

              <div class="recall-memo-card">
                <div class="rmc-icon"><svg><use href="#icon-compass"/></svg></div>
                <div class="rmc-body">
                  <div class="rmc-kicker"><span class="k-type">decision</span><span class="k-tag">#api-v3</span></div>
                  <div class="rmc-title">Auth refactor held pending token-rotation review</div>
                </div>
                <div class="rmc-meta">Mar 12</div>
              </div>

              <div class="recall-memo-card">
                <div class="rmc-icon"><svg><use href="#icon-bookopen"/></svg></div>
                <div class="rmc-body">
                  <div class="rmc-kicker"><span class="k-type">context</span><span class="k-tag">#mobile-platform</span></div>
                  <div class="rmc-title">Session migration needs device-bound refresh handling</div>
                </div>
                <div class="rmc-meta">Apr 02</div>
              </div>
            </Message>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================
     OPEN SOURCE — built in the open, forkable, self-hostable
     Inspiration: t3.chat, Cal.com, Plausible, Supabase — leading
     with openness as a feature, not a footnote. Tone is
     dev-credible (real commands, real claims) without star-count
     theatre we don't have yet on day one.
     ============================================================ -->
<div class="frame warm" id="open-source">
  <div class="memo-shell">
    <div class="feature-band media-left">
      <div class="band-media" data-decorative>
        <div class="os-terminal" aria-label="Clone and run Threa locally.">
          <span class="row"><span class="prompt">$</span><span class="cmd">git clone</span> <span class="arg">github.com/threahq/threa.git</span></span>
          <span class="row"><span class="prompt">$</span><span class="cmd">cd</span> <span class="arg">threa</span> <span class="cmd">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class="cmd">bun install</span></span>
          <span class="row"><span class="prompt">$</span><span class="cmd">bun run dev</span></span>
          <span class="out">→ http://localhost:5173</span>
          <span class="row"><span class="cmt"># your machine. your fork.</span></span>
        </div>

        <figure class="patch-example" aria-label="Patch Threa by describing the change to your own agent.">
          <figcaption><span class="file">patch.md</span><span class="hint">describe the change</span></figcaption>
          <div class="patch-body">
            <span class="ln md-h"># Compact density toggle</span>
            <span class="ln md-p">Add a "Compact" option under Settings → Appearance.</span>
            <span class="ln md-li">- add a `density` pref: comfortable | compact</span>
            <span class="ln md-li">- compact tightens message-row padding and line-height</span>
            <span class="ln md-li">- persist per-device; default to comfortable</span>
            <span class="ln md-li">- apply it in the timeline, threads, and scratchpads</span>
          </div>
          <div class="patch-run"><span class="prompt">$</span><span class="cmd">claude</span> -p <span class="arg">"$(cat patch.md)"</span></div>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="band-copy">
        <h2>It's open source.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          The frontend, backend, control plane, and infrastructure are all
          public, and the public repo is the one we deploy. Read exactly how
          Threa works, fork it, or run it yourself. Do whatever.
        </p>

        <div class="os-tenets">
          <div class="os-tenet">
            <h4>All of it is on GitHub</h4>
            <p>
              The code, data model, access checks, model calls, and deployment
              setup.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="os-tenet">
            <h4>MIT licensed</h4>
            <p>
              Fork it, change the product, or run your own version on the same
              code we ship. I won't take it personally.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="os-tenet">
            <h4>Built in the open</h4>
            <p>
              Design docs, implementation plans, and the feature list are
              public too. Embarrassing drafts included.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a class="os-cta" href="https://github.com/threahq/threa">Browse the source on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================
     BRING YOUR OWN AGENT — data portability + BYO agent
     The contrarian beat: every other platform is racing to lock
     you into their built-in agent. Threa ships a good one
     (Ariadne) AND makes it trivial to walk your memory over to
     the agent you already pay for. The starter-motor framing is
     the headline idea.
     ============================================================ -->
<div class="frame" id="byo-agent">
  <div class="memo-shell byo-shell">
    <div class="byo-copy">
      <h2>Bring the agent you already use.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Threa ships with Ariadne, and she's useful from day one. But you probably
        already have an agent set up the way you like it, with your codebase and
        your context. Connect that one as a Threa bot instead of starting over
        with mine. It can even stay on your laptop behind NAT.
      </p>
      <p class="lede byo-lede">
        Mention the bot in a channel and the runtime hands the request to your
        local agent, then posts the reply under the bot's name. It can search
        messages by text or meaning, read memos and attachments, and follow a
        memo back to the conversation it came from. It can also take whole
        tasks. You delegate, watch it work in the stream, and the finished thing
        lands where the team can see it.
      </p>
      <p class="lede byo-lede">
        Some of that work shouldn't be readable by anyone but you and your agent.
        Put it in a <a href="/encryption">sealed scratchpad</a> and it is encrypted
        on your devices before it ever reaches Threa.
      </p>

      <p class="byo-works">
        Works today with Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, OpenCode, Gemini CLI, or a bot
        you write yourself, through the bot runtime, the CLI, or the MCP server.
      </p>
      <a class="os-cta" href="/developers/recipes#local-agent">Connect a local agent</a>
    </div>
    <div class="byo-demo" data-decorative>
      <div class="ad" aria-label="Alex asks their Claude Code bot in #api-v3 whether token rotation still signs out old sessions">
        <div class="ad-head">
          <span class="ad-channel">#api-v3</span>
          <span class="ad-chip" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg><use href="#spinner-icon"/></svg>
            <span>Claude Code</span>
            <span class="ad-chip-steps">· <span class="ad-steps">1 step</span></span>
          </span>
        </div>

        <!-- Bottom-anchored like a real stream: an arriving row grows in at the
             foot and pushes older rows up under the top fade. -->
        <div class="ad-log">
          <Message author="maya" time="14:00" ago={14}>
            <div class="tl-text">v3 release branch is cut, aiming to ship Thursday.</div>
          </Message>

          <Message author="jordan" time="14:00" ago={11}>
            <div class="tl-text">changelog draft is up, only the auth section left</div>
          </Message>

          <Message author="maya" time="14:01" ago={6}>
            <div class="tl-text">Before we ship v3: does token rotation still sign out sessions issued before the migration?</div>
          </Message>

          <Message author="jordan" time="14:03" ago={4}>
            <div class="tl-text">no idea, I'd have to dig through the rotation code again</div>
          </Message>

          <div class="ad-in" data-beat="sent"><div>
            <Message author="alex" time="14:07" ago={0}>
              <div class="tl-text"><span class="mention">@claude-code</span> can you check?</div>
            </Message>
          </div></div>

          <!-- Same card as the app's AgentSessionEvent: a live substep with a
               pulse dot while running, swapped in place for the summary. -->
          <div class="ad-in" data-beat="working"><div>
            <div class="trace-card ad-trace">
              <div class="trace-icon-slot">
                <div class="trace-icon trace-icon-running" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#spinner-icon"/></svg></div>
                <div class="trace-icon trace-icon-done" aria-hidden="true"><svg><use href="#check-icon"/></svg></div>
              </div>
              <div class="ad-trace-main">
                <div class="ad-trace-title">Claude Code is working…</div>
                <div class="ad-trace-sub">
                  <span class="ad-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span class="ad-substep">Searching messages for “token rotation”</span>
                  <span class="ad-trace-count">· <span class="ad-steps">1 step</span></span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="trace-time" data-ago="0">14:07</div>
            </div>
          </div></div>

          <div class="ad-in" data-beat="replied"><div>
            <Message author="claude-code" time="14:07" ago={0}>
              <div class="tl-text">Yes. Sessions from before the migration keep their old refresh token, so the first rotation signs them out. Jordan flagged exactly this when v3 was held:</div>
              <div class="quote-card">
